+-- =====================================================================
+-- PRODUCTION RELEASE: GUARDED. This migration is applied to local and CI
+-- databases only. It must reach a hosted database through the guarded
+-- production release (preflight, postflight, receipt), never as a side
+-- effect of a merge. It follows 20261025400000, and 20260907081757,
+-- 20260907111757 and 20261016181000, whose three bodies it patches in place.
+-- =====================================================================
+--
+-- G8.5, Copilot for an adult's own record (owner decision of 19 November
+-- 2026, "G8.5: Copilot for an adult's own record is built"). The signed
+-- register already allows it: policyResolvers.scope-derived-v1, subject:adult,
+-- principalRelationshipCases.own-subject, for a local model (copilot.local)
+-- and an approved cloud provider (copilot.cloud and the cloud-model consent
+-- for the exact provider, recipient revision and subject,
+-- cloud-model-consent-v1 scopeRequirements.subject:own-adult). Until now the
+-- own Copilot permission and authority admitted a self subject only
+-- (public.own_report_context_v1 requires subject_class 'self'), so an adult
+-- record the person holds in their own account answered not-found.
+--
+-- "Held by the person themselves" is decided here, from database rows only:
+--   * the record is other_adult, its subject_account_id is the acting
+--     account, no account owns it (owner_account_id is null, so it is neither
+--     a Path B record an uploader owns nor a transferred one), it is active,
+--     its analysis was never stopped and it belongs to no cohort;
+--   * the account holds the record's current adult_claim binding, which only
+--     Path A's account acceptance writes, with the record's active
+--     account_subject principal;
+--   * the invitation for it was accepted, and the person's own
+--     consent.subject-adult acceptance signature by that principal, on the
+--     current artifact, carries an unrevoked adult_source consent;
+--   * and every check the self context makes holds for the record itself:
+--     private.own_upload_store_authority_v1 (a live session of this account,
+--     an adult, unbanned account, the binding and principal, and the record's
+--     own consent.upload-self and insurance acknowledgement at that binding).
+-- other-adult-mitigation-state-v1, as far as this deployment records it: a
+-- public appeal holding the record denies every read, as
+-- private.other_adult_mitigation_v1 denies it first. The 72-hour hold for an
+-- account created from the invitation, its independent boundary notice and
+-- the 30-day re-notice have no mechanism yet (Path A answers every acceptance
+-- existing_account) and are not enforced here.
+--
+--   1. private.own_copilot_context_v1 returns exactly what
+--      public.own_report_context_v1 returns for a self subject (it calls it),
+--      and the same context for an adult record held as above. Every other
+--      subject is 42501 not_found. Owner-only: only the definer functions
+--      below call it.
+--   2. private.own_copilot_configuration_v1 resolves its context through it.
+--      Patched in place, md5-guarded with its exact reviewed ACL. Everything
+--      built on it is unchanged and now serves that record too: the
+--      presentation, grant, authority, revocation (and its nonce door), the
+--      chat with its server-held conversation, revoke-all and the export's
+--      chat reader. A conversation is stored as every own conversation is,
+--      scope_kind 'self' with the record's subject_id.
+--   3. private.own_report_purge_scope_v1 admits a Copilot grant on such a
+--      record, so withdrawing it, superseding it on a settings change,
+--      revoke-all and deleting the record queue the exact purge of the
+--      conversation turns it authorized, as they do for a self subject.
+--      Without this the revocation trigger refuses and nothing could be
+--      withdrawn.
+--   4. private.purge_path_a_subject_v1 (api.subject-delete's Path A case)
+--      deletes the record's conversations with their model working state, as
+--      private.empty_self_subject_v1 does for a self record, and refuses if
+--      any turn that retrieved the record would remain.
